20:["$","$L31",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L32",null,{"title":"I want to add a store. Which crates do I touch?","id":"which-crates-for-a-store","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Two, plus a Bazel file: the spec goes in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config"}],", the\nimplementation and its factory arm go in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-store"}],", and the new\nfile has to be added to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-store/BUILD.bazel"}],". The step-by-step\nis in ",["$","$L2f",null,{"href":"/contribute/how-to-extend#adding-a-store","children":"how to extend"}],"."]}]}],["$","$L32",null,{"title":"Why is there no `members` list in the workspace?","id":"no-members-list","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Membership is derived from the root package's path dependencies. It\nworks, and it means the dependency graph and the workspace definition\ncannot drift apart, but it does mean a crate nothing depends on is\nsilently not in the workspace."}]}],["$","$L32",null,{"title":"Can I build without Bazel?","id":"build-without-bazel","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Yes. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cargo build --all"}]," builds the whole workspace. CI runs Bazel as\nwell, and a few checks exist only there, so run ",["$","code",null,{"children":"bazel test //..."}]," before\nsubmitting. See ",["$","$L2f",null,{"href":"/contribute/testing-guide","children":"the testing guide"}],"."]}]}],["$","$L32",null,{"title":"Where does `main()` live?","id":"where-is-main","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"src/bin/forge.rs"}],", in the root package. It builds the Tokio runtime\nby hand, constructs the stores, then assembles the gRPC routes. It is the\nsingle best file to read first if you want to see how the pieces connect."]}]}]]}]
